From 4ed2497eaff8785673234a5e7b61cb2a1170d7d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:12:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: D2R's lighting table blur with 8 cells per thread, fewer
 shared memory reads

fex31's 4-cell version of D2R's compute shader 83e2eb4a6bf5f03b took
8.5 ms per run on the Adreno 740 (2 cells: 10.4 ms, fex30: 12-13 ms).
Over the three versions the run time grows with the shared memory reads
per summed product (one in the 4-cell version), not with the
instruction count, so shared memory reads are the limit now.

Two new versions, both summing 8 cells per thread:
- 4 x by 2 y (local size 2x4x8, fex_shader_swap_83e2.comp). When
  A = 2 W (D2R), cell x + 1 reads at i the s2 value cell x reads at
  i - 2, so the last 8 s2 values stay in registers and each one read
  serves all four x: 3 shared memory reads per 8 products.
- 8 x in a row (local size 1x8x8, fex_shader_swap_83e2_row.comp), the
  last 16 s2 values in registers: 2 reads per 8 products.
For 32 i per step the sums are straight-line code in which every read
names a fixed register (as a loop, the compiler copied the window and
the sums each pass). The s1 samples are turned into (x+w, y+w, z+w, w)
only when stored one step later: fex31 waited for the texture unit
right after each s1 sample. The s2 table has 48 slots per z (46 used in
D2R), so a group takes 10 KB of shared memory (3 groups per core).
Host Turnip (fex16): 48 registers, no spills, about 1,450 issue cycles
per 256 products and step (fex31's 4-cell version: about 1,900).
Both match the game's shader up to float rounding on lavapipe (16
table sizes and the fallback path, largest relative difference 5e-6).

VKD3D_FEX_SHADER_SWAP keeps its values: alt (default) = binds take
turns between both, 1 = 4 x by 2 y only, 2 = 8 in a row only, 0 = the
game's shader.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WZVGoVEaHJ78mpf2D3MiER
